-- `fmt` is variadic but does NOT splat lists. Passing a list literal to
-- a multi-`{}` template silently mis-fills (pre-0.12.1): the list bound
-- to the first slot and the rest were left as literal `{}`.
--
--   fmt "x={} y={}" [10, 20]    -- WRONG: "x=[10, 20] y={}"
--
-- 0.12.1 catches this at verify with ILO-T013 (slot/arg-count mismatch).
-- Two idiomatic shapes:
--   1. positional args  -> fmt "x={} y={}" 10 20
--   2. single-slot list -> fmt "list={}" [10, 20]   (formats list as one value)

-- positional: one `{}` per value
both-positional>t;fmt "x={} y={}" 10 20

-- single-slot: list rendered as a single value
list-as-one>t;fmt "list={}" [10, 20]

-- run: both-positional
-- out: x=10 y=20
-- run: list-as-one
-- out: list=[10, 20]
